Mark the start and the end of each startup phase

The boot freezes right after vm_fault_init() prints the compressor mode, which
vm_mem_bootstrap() calls just before kernel_startup_initialize_upto(
STARTUP_SUB_ZALLOC).  So the stall is inside the ZALLOC phase, but the console
is a 40-line overwrite buffer and is never cleared, so the phase markers in a
photo cannot be ordered reliably against the older boot lines still on screen.

Print a marker when a phase starts as well as when it ends.  B7 with no E7
after it means the phase began and never finished; E7 with no B7 means the
phase finished and the stall is in whatever runs next.  Two lines per phase,
about sixteen in total, so the panel stays readable.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -433,3 +433,6 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 	assert(startup_phase < upto);
 
+	if (upto >= STARTUP_SUB_KPRINTF) {
+		printf("\nB%u", (unsigned)upto);
+	}
 	while (cur < startup_entries_end && cur->subsystem <= upto) {
@@ -444,3 +447,6 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 		startup_entry_cur = ++cur;
 	}
+	if (upto >= STARTUP_SUB_KPRINTF) {
+		printf("\nE%u", (unsigned)upto);
+	}
 	kernel_startup_log(upto);
